Expected elements: present

Presence check passes. Provenance banner (badge, tone, `aztec` slug, four producer sentences) sits first, above a slim identity bar carrying `← aztec`, the truncated hash, `Partial`, block, both stepping directions, scrubber, `128 / 1315`, phase rail and the `NOIR` tag. Code pane with line 32 marked, Call Trace/Event Log as one tab strip with Call Trace open, Values as a pane below it, Transaction pane. No spinner, no empty pane, no full-width pane row, no prose band between bar and panes.

Typographically the page is competent — mono for identifiers, sans for paths, right-aligned tabular opcode counts, a good syntax palette, and a designed fade mask on horizontal overflow. What it lacks is a working label level. The 10px letterspaced uppercase style carries six roles at once, so `TRANSACTION` reads at exactly the rank of `BLOCK`, `FINALITY` and `FEE PAYER` inside it. Above that, the provenance paragraph is set at explorer scale (~15px sans, 4 lines) and is the loudest type on a debugger screen. Numbers disagree with themselves: `1,315` in the call trace, `1315` in the identity bar for the same total, `10000` and `88000 / 200000` elsewhere. Hashes are truncated three different ways, including a mid-string wrap on FEE PAYER and TARGET.

Highest-priority fixes: give the pane title a rank its own field labels do not share, and set the banner at the debugger's type scale. Second: one thousands-separator rule and one hash-truncation rule product-wide.

Rating: 6/10

